{"c":[{"id":"22bae55a2a60fd23","sum":"B19-B20: undoing a skill run resets its clean count; a per-pid listen-only tap sees clicks posted to that pid; background-only caret-fixture takes no posted click (use --foreground); pid-posted input resets HIDIdleTime, so GUI evals log their last post.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"d9542f01119cf37d","sum":"B19-B20: undoing a skill run resets its clean count. A listen-only tap per pid sees clicks posted to that pid (global monitor and session tap do not); a background-only caret-fixture takes no posted click, --foreground (accessory) does.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T221243Z-e77935deee83e487","text":"Skills (B19): undoing a skill run resets its clean count, so a fixture forced-mismatch run with no Tab needs ten more clean runs after run 11's undo. Live Jev's first naming ask fell under NAME_CUTOFF 0.5 in 7 of 9 tries; the reworded retry picked.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T234914Z-795f3dcc958c0f2c","text":"A listen-only tap per pid sees clicks posted to that pid; the global NSEvent monitor and a session tap do not (B20, 6 of 6 vs 0 of 6). A background-only caret-fixture takes no posted click and cannot hit-test a covered window; --foreground (accessory) does both.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"e619089820dda277","sum":"B20: input posted to a pid resets HIDIdleTime like a person's, so GUI evals record their last post (scripts/synthetic-input.ts) or the idle gate stops them. TextEdit cannot host a routine: one text area, no positions, one value per field.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T234914Z-993bc2a42fa75599","text":"Input posted to a pid (CGEventPostToPid) resets HIDIdleTime like a person's (B20: 196 s to 0.3 s); GUI evals that post input record their last post (helper/scripts/synthetic-input.ts) or the idle gate stops them as 'user back'.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T234914Z-ac2ee9392ce81473","text":"TextEdit cannot host a B19 routine: a shape is (source template, part, destination template) with no positions, a document is one text area, values copied from list lines share one source template, and engine.plan writes one value per field (B20).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"f76396784bf60827","sum":"B20-B21: a closing window can reach the model fieldless; routines use last-seen places. Evals starting Electron drop ELECTRON_RUN_AS_NODE. A non-key WKWebView writes AXValue to the focused field (reader: focusValue). Shadow keys are hashes, so real-day-replay counts approximate.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"a097a19063cce23e","sum":"B20: a closing window can reach the model without its fields before its close, so routines place late edits from where elements were last seen; the agent host sets ELECTRON_RUN_AS_NODE, so an eval starting Electron must drop it.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T004204Z-5758654235cf32d7","text":"A closing window (Chrome tearing down its page, a Send that closes it) can reach the model without its fields before its close; routines place late edits and presses from where elements were last seen, or Caret's verified runs score as misses (B20).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T004204Z-584e781bcb96f4a6","text":"The agent host sets ELECTRON_RUN_AS_NODE for its children; an eval that starts Electron must drop it or Electron runs as plain Node and cannot require('electron') (B20).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"70fc0cfcbac83876","sum":"B20-B21: a non-key WKWebView applies an AXValue write to the focused field, so the reader focuses a web field first (focusValue); the shadow store keeps keys only as hashes, so real-day-replay counts approximate and memory.sqlite routine rows are exact.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T004204Z-9249ce81a51a9397","text":"WKWebView in a window that is not key applies an AXValue write to whichever field has focus (none: dropped; another: overwritten). The reader focuses a WebKit web field first (focusValue): 3/3 landed, no raise or activation; typing or paste to the pid land 0/3 (B20).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T015937Z-03e29f7fee084743","text":"The shadow store keeps element keys only as hashes, so an offline replay cannot recover templates or positions; scripts/real-day-replay.ts counts are approximations both ways; memory.sqlite routine rows are the faithful count (B21).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]}
